.TH GIT-MAIL 1 "2024" "git-mail 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-mail \- Terminal-based, offline-first email client using Git storage
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-mail
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-mail
is a terminal-based email client that stores emails as plain-text files in a Git repository. It treats email management like code development - versioned, scriptable, and portable. Each email is stored as an individual file, and all operations are performed using shell scripts and command-line tools.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose logging output
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIFILE\fR
Specify configuration file path (default: ~/.git-mail/config.toml)
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-\-repo " " \fIPATH\fR
Specify repository path (default: ~/.git-mail)
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help information
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version information
.SH COMMANDS
.SS Repository Management
.TP
.B init [\fIPATH\fR]
Initialize a new Git-Mail repository. Creates the directory structure, Git repository, and default configuration files.
.SS Interactive Interface
.TP
.B tui
Start the terminal user interface for interactive email management. Provides a full-screen interface with keyboard navigation.
.SS Email Operations
.TP
.B sync [\fIACCOUNT\fR]
Synchronize emails with configured accounts. Fetches new emails and sends queued outbound messages.
.TP
.B compose [\fB--to\fR \fIEMAIL\fR] [\fB--subject\fR \fISUBJECT\fR]
Compose a new email using your configured text editor.
.TP
.B reply \fIEMAIL_ID\fR [\fB--account\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR]
Reply to an existing email with quoted content and proper threading.
.TP
.B forward \fIEMAIL_ID\fR [\fB--account\fR \fIACCOUNT\fR]
Forward an email to other recipients, preserving attachments.
.SS Email Browsing
.TP
.B list [\fIFOLDER\fR] [\fB--count\fR \fIN\fR]
List emails in a folder with summary information (sender, subject, date).
.TP
.B show \fIEMAIL_ID\fR
Display the full content of an email including headers and body.
.TP
.B search \fIQUERY\fR [\fB--folder\fR \fIFOLDER\fR]
Search through emails using grep-based pattern matching.
.SS Draft Management
.TP
.B draft list
List all draft emails
.TP
.B draft show \fIID\fR
Display draft content
.TP
.B draft edit \fIID\fR
Edit a draft in your text editor
.TP
.B draft send \fIID\fR
Send a draft email
.TP
.B draft delete \fIID\fR
Delete a draft email
.SS Account Management
.TP
.B account list
List all configured email accounts
.TP
.B account add \fINAME\fR
Add a new email account with interactive setup
.TP
.B account remove \fINAME\fR
Remove an email account and its configuration
.TP
.B account test \fINAME\fR
Test connection to an email account
.SS Plugin System
.TP
.B plugin list
List available plugins
.TP
.B plugin execute \fINAME\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Execute a plugin with optional arguments
.TP
.B plugin info \fINAME\fR
Show detailed information about a plugin
.TP
.B plugin reload
Reload plugins from plugin directories
.SS External Tools
.TP
.B tool pipe \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...] \fB--emails\fR \fIIDS\fR
Pipe email content to an external command
.TP
.B tool grep \fIPATTERN\fR \fB--emails\fR \fIIDS\fR
Search through specified emails using grep
.TP
.B tool awk \fISCRIPT\fR \fB--emails\fR \fIIDS\fR
Process emails using awk scripts
.TP
.B tool count \fB--emails\fR \fIIDS\fR [\fB--count-type\fR \fITYPE\fR]
Count lines, words, or characters in emails
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Getting Started
Initialize a new repository:
.RS
.B git-mail init
.RE

Add your first email account:
.RS
.B git-mail account add personal
.RE

Sync your emails:
.RS
.B git-mail sync
.RE

Start the interactive interface:
.RS
.B git-mail tui
.RE

.SS Email Management
List emails in inbox:
.RS
.B git-mail list
.RE

Show a specific email:
.RS
.B git-mail show abc123def
.RE

Compose a new email:
.RS
.B git-mail compose --to colleague@company.com --subject "Meeting Tomorrow"
.RE

Reply to an email:
.RS
.B git-mail reply abc123def
.RE

Search for emails:
.RS
.B git-mail search "project deadline"
.RE

.SS Advanced Usage
Search in specific folder:
.RS
.B git-mail search "urgent" --folder work
.RE

Pipe emails to external tools:
.RS
.B git-mail tool pipe sort --emails abc123,def456
.RE

Execute custom plugins:
.RS
.B git-mail plugin execute backup --full
.RE

.SH CONFIGURATION
Git-Mail uses TOML configuration files located in the repository directory:

.TP
.B config.toml
Main configuration file containing global settings
.TP
.B accounts/
Directory containing individual account configurations
.TP
.B filters/
Directory containing email filter scripts
.TP
.B plugins/
Directory containing custom plugin scripts

.SH REPOSITORY STRUCTURE
Git-Mail organizes emails in a structured directory layout:

.TP
.B inbox/
Incoming emails organized by date
.TP
.B sent/
Sent emails organized by date
.TP
.B drafts/
Draft emails being composed
.TP
.B archive/
Archived emails
.TP
.B [custom-folders]/
User-created organizational folders

Each email is stored as a plain-text file with RFC 2822 formatting, and all changes are tracked in Git history.

.SH ENVIRONMENT VARIABLES
.TP
.B EDITOR
Text editor used for composing emails (default: vi)
.TP
.B GIT_MAIL_HOME
Override default repository location
.TP
.B GIT_MAIL_CONFIG
Override default configuration file location

.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.git-mail/
Default repository and configuration directory
.TP
.B ~/.git-mail/config.toml
Main configuration file
.TP
.B ~/.git-mail/accounts/
Account configuration directory
.TP
.B ~/.git-mail/filters/
Email filter scripts directory
.TP
.B ~/.git-mail/plugins/
Custom plugin scripts directory

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success
.TP
.B 1
General error
.TP
.B 2
Configuration error
.TP
.B 3
Network error
.TP
.B 4
Authentication error

